00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.340
Are you as sick of winning as I am at this
point?

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.860
OK, now let's talk about Corona virus more
broadly and what's going on.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.139
So we will do.

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.820
I'm not doing these daily anymore, but I'm
sort of doing these weekly or as the data

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.240
requires, the big picture on Corona virus
is it's really, really bad here in the United

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.240
States.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.240
A lot of the world has already figured out.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.340
January 20th, we got our first case.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.450
South Korea got their first case.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:28.600
They still have under 300 total deaths at
the last I checked.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.300
We are obviously doing much, much worse than
that.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.240
Around one hundred and twenty five thousand
deaths in total right now in terms of cases.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.070
We are setting new records in terms of new
cases in the United States.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:49.329
We had almost 60000 new cases in a single
day on July 2nd, about 55000 cases on July

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:51.809
3rd, some lower numbers over the weekend.

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:55.070
Typically, over weekends and holiday weekends,
the numbers decrease.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:00.860
So we could have today and tomorrow some huge
numbers as a result of catching up on underreporting

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.860
over the weekend.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.360
Now, a good thing is that death numbers are
down.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:12.610
There's this growing idea on the right that
the evil left, the Marxist socialist left,

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.430
doesn't want to admit that deaths are down
despite cases being up.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.791
Oh, I'm readily admitting it.

00:01:18.791 --> 00:01:21.990
And there's about five or six different possibilities
about why it's going on.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.230
I don't want a single person to die.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.560
I don't want a single person to get coronavirus.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.000
And I hope that that continues.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.930
And we'll talk about why that may be going
on.

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:35.100
And a little bit in terms of cases, the hot
spots are Florida, Texas, California remains

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.100
a hot spot.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.760
Georgia, Arizona, the Carolinas, Tennessee,
it's mostly red states, plus California.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.720
Florida set a major record with the most new
cases in a single week of any state since

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.240
the start of the pandemic.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.200
They had over fifty nine thousand cases in
a seven day period last week.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.440
The Phenix Arizona mayor has admitted they
opened up too early.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.229
This is not the Republican governor of Arizona.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:01.380
This is merely merely an important person.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.360
But what I mean is they are speaking only
from their democratic perspective.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.600
As mayor of Phenix, take a look at this.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.200
We opened way too early in Arizona.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.849
We were one of the last states to go to stay
at home and one of the first to reemerged.

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:17.800
And we reemerged at zero to 60.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.130
We had crowded nightclubs handing out free
champagne.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:28.890
No masks are 20 to forty four year olds, which
is my own demographic, really led the explosion.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.780
And we've seen such growth in that area.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:36.190
We're seeing a lot of people go to large family
gatherings and in fact, their family members.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.610
We are in a crisis related to testing.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:43.430
I was visiting a testing facility this weekend
and people waiting still eight hours.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.800
Good for her for admitting it.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.570
Friends of mine in Arizona say it's an insane
situation.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:53.209
Hospital capacity is rapidly filling up in
Texas.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:59.769
University of Texas Austin researchers expect
hospitals in Texas are in in Austin, rather,

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:02.790
will be over capacity potentially by the end
of the month.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.890
The mayor of Austin says they're in trouble.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.130
And a reality we're learning is.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:12.019
So we learned early that governors have to
deal with the reality on the ground, whereas

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:13.019
Trump doesn't.

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:16.540
Trump can just say, we're putting out the
embers and everything's going great.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.690
Governors have to deal with the real situation.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.060
Some of the governors choose to ignore the
reality.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.850
Like, for example, we saw this in Texas.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:24.430
We're seeing it in Florida.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:30.540
Arizona mayors doubly have to deal with the
realities that sometimes governors don't have

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.540
to deal with.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.800
How many of our hospitals are full right now?

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.200
Do we have to start telling people in Phenix
that they've got to maybe go to Tucson if

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.050
they want to, if they need an ICU bed, for
example?

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.720
So mayors are increasingly sounding the alarm.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.830
Now, let's get back to this question.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:51.020
Why are deaths so low compared to these new
case numbers?

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:55.440
Because when you look at the case numbers,
we're having now bigger than we've ever had

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.440
before.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.909
The death numbers are only a fraction of what
we were having in April and early May.

00:04:00.909 --> 00:04:01.909
That's a good thing.

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:05.659
We don't want people tonight to die, but we
want to know why this is going on.

00:04:05.659 --> 00:04:06.849
Deaths continue to trend down.

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:10.820
So there's a few possibilities we've discussed,
all of which are still on the table.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:17.669
One is that there's just a lag between cases
and deaths as the hospitals get better at

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:20.189
treating people earlier in the disease.

00:04:20.189 --> 00:04:22.139
It may take even longer to.

00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:25.689
Be very sort of dark for people to die.

00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:29.990
And so the deaths haven't yet happened from
a lot of these early cases.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:35.999
The ideas you need about 19 to 21 days for
a case to become a death if it's going to

00:04:35.999 --> 00:04:37.599
we're on day 17 right now.

00:04:37.599 --> 00:04:43.580
So if the explanation is that we just haven't
seen the deaths yet from these new cases,

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:47.439
we would expect the deaths to spike sometime
in the middle or the end of this week.

00:04:47.439 --> 00:04:48.680
We're going to watch that.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.639
Another hypothesizes there's now a less deadly
strain, which may be more contagious.

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:55.919
In other words, it spreads more easily.

00:04:55.919 --> 00:04:58.259
But it is less severe.

00:04:58.259 --> 00:05:00.819
So it will cause fewer deaths per case.

00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:01.819
That's an assertion.

00:05:01.819 --> 00:05:03.430
We've not seen actual evidence of that yet.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.050
We want to be careful.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:07.909
Number three, some states could just be lying.

00:05:07.909 --> 00:05:12.240
I mean, that that's the the you know, it's
it's a very simplistic explanation.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.009
But from what we've seen in Florida and some
other states, it's possible states are seeing

00:05:17.009 --> 00:05:19.830
more deaths, but they're simply lying about
it.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.569
Again, we need evidence to really believe
that.

00:05:22.569 --> 00:05:27.199
The fourth possibility is that increasingly
it's younger people now testing positive.

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:31.189
So even though the total case numbers are
going up, the number of people in the high

00:05:31.189 --> 00:05:36.599
risk age groups are less likely to be getting
it now because they're staying home.

00:05:36.599 --> 00:05:41.300
And so a lot of these young cases are not
ultimately going to lead to deaths.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:47.610
Number five is increase testing means that
in general, you have less sick people getting

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.840
tests at an earlier point.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:54.559
Tests were so difficult to come by that you
they were really restricted to people who

00:05:54.559 --> 00:05:56.310
were much more ill.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:02.499
Now, in those case numbers, you have people,
but you're capturing more of the cases and

00:06:02.499 --> 00:06:04.639
a lot of those cases are less severe.

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:06.330
That's a possibility.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:10.939
And the number six is some combination of
these factors and or something that we don't

00:06:10.939 --> 00:06:11.939
yet know.

00:06:11.939 --> 00:06:13.490
So we're going to keep watching it.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.080
I have no desire to see deaths go up for political
reasons.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:21.539
As I've already told you, the case for removing
Donald Trump is crystal clear without a single

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:22.929
